1
00:00:01,260 --> 00:00:01,940
Reading

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:06,120
The True North, from Toronto to Montreal.

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:13,060
The next morning the bushes and maple trees outside their windows were red, gold and orange,

4
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:17,340
and there was frost on the ground, confirming that fall had arrived in Canada.

5
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:20,340
Around noon they arrived in Toronto,

6
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:23,120
the biggest and most wealthy city in Canada.

7
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:27,280
They were not leaving for Montreal until later,

8
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:29,140
so they went on a tour of the city.

9
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:38,520
In the distance, they could see the misty cloud that rose from the great Niagara Falls,

10
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:40,740
which is on the south side of the lake.

11
00:00:41,480 --> 00:00:46,240
The water flows into the Niagara River and over the falls on its way to the sea.

12
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:51,440
They saw the covered stadium, home of several famous basketball teams.

13
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:02,180
I should phone her from a telephone booth."

14
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:06,900
They met Lin Fei around dusk in downtown Chinatown,

15
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:08,880
one of the three in Toronto.

16
00:01:09,940 --> 00:01:12,940
Over dinner at a restaurant called The Pink Pearl,

17
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:15,120
the cousins chatted with Lin Fei,

18
00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:18,000
who had moved to Canada many years earlier.

19
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:22,640
We can get good Cantonese food here," Lin Fei told them, "

20
00:01:22,680 --> 00:01:25,900
because most of the Chinese people here come from South China,

21
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:27,560
especially Hong Kong.

22
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:30,480
It’s too bad you can’t go as far as Ottawa,

23
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:31,600
Canada’s capital.

24
00:01:44,460 --> 00:01:47,500
At the station, people everywhere were speaking French.

25
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:56,800
We don’t leave until this evening," said Liu Qian.

26
00:01:57,480 --> 00:01:58,480
Let’s go downtown.

27
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:04,520
Old Montreal is close to the water." They spent the afternoon in lovely shops

28
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:07,640
and visiting artists in their workplaces beside the water.

29
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:12,660
As they sat in a buffet restaurant looking over the broad St Lawrence River,

30
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:15,400
a young man sat down with them.

31
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:17,300
Hello, my name is Henri.

32
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:21,140
I’m a student at the university nearby," he said, "

33
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:23,560
and I was wondering where you are from."

34
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:27,540
The girls told him they were on a train trip across Canada

35
00:02:27,540 --> 00:02:30,240
and that they had only one day in Montreal.

36
00:02:31,180 --> 00:02:33,100
That’s too bad," he said.

37
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:36,400
Montreal is a city with wonderful restaurants and clubs.

38
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:39,220
Most of us speak both English and French,

39
00:02:39,220 --> 00:02:41,980
but the city has French culture and traditions.

40
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:45,880
We love good coffee, good bread and good music."

41
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:51,960
That night as the train was speeding along the St Lawrence River toward the Gulf of St Lawrence

42
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:54,320
and down to the distant east coast,

43
00:02:55,060 --> 00:02:58,680
the cousins dreamed of French restaurants and red maple leaves.
